// Go workspace spanning the three modules.
//
// They are separate modules, not packages of one, so the boundaries are enforced
// by the compiler rather than by convention:
//
//   packages/proto  the device-plane contract, imported by both binaries
//   apps/server     the management server
//   apps/agent      the macOS agent
//
// The agent physically CANNOT import apps/server/internal — Go's internal rule
// blocks it across module boundaries. That matters: the agent ships to customer
// hardware, and a shared internal package is exactly how a server dependency
// ends up on 10,000 Macs.

go 1.25.0

use (
	./apps/agent
	./apps/server
	./packages/proto
)
